1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:03,507
This is SecureSignal.

2
00:00:03,507 --> 00:00:07,182
Confidential portfolio intelligence, built on Flare

3
00:00:07,182 --> 00:00:08,738
Confidential Compute.

4
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:11,737
Getting personalized crypto advice today means

5
00:00:11,737 --> 00:00:15,042
handing your full holdings to a centralized service

6
00:00:15,042 --> 00:00:16,186
you cannot audit.

7
00:00:16,186 --> 00:00:19,724
That exposes you to front-running, privacy leaks,

8
00:00:19,724 --> 00:00:21,281
and targeted attacks.

9
00:00:21,281 --> 00:00:25,171
SecureSignal runs the analysis entirely inside a

10
00:00:25,171 --> 00:00:28,346
Trusted Execution Environment on Flare.

11
00:00:28,346 --> 00:00:31,804
Your data is encrypted in the browser, decrypted

12
00:00:31,804 --> 00:00:35,333
only inside the enclave, and every result carries

13
00:00:35,333 --> 00:00:37,803
a verifiable on-chain attestation.

14
00:00:37,803 --> 00:00:39,596
Not even we can see your data.

15
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,499
Here is how it works.

16
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:44,950
The frontend generates a one-time session key, and

17
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:48,401
encrypts your portfolio with the TEE's public key.

18
00:00:48,401 --> 00:00:52,163
A registry contract on the Coston2 testnet records

19
00:00:52,163 --> 00:00:55,113
the task and the TEE's attestation key.

20
00:00:55,113 --> 00:00:58,400
Inside the enclave, the TEE node decrypts the

21
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:02,044
payload, runs the risk analysis, signs the result,

22
00:01:02,044 --> 00:01:05,045
and encrypts it back to your session key.

23
00:01:05,045 --> 00:01:08,646
Finally, the app verifies the signature, and the

24
00:01:08,646 --> 00:01:10,263
on-chain result hash.

25
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:11,763
Let's see it live.

26
00:01:11,763 --> 00:01:14,760
I connect my wallet on the Coston2 testnet,

27
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:16,804
and enter a sample portfolio.

28
00:01:16,804 --> 00:01:19,792
When I click run, the app encrypts everything

29
00:01:19,792 --> 00:01:23,040
locally, nothing leaves the browser in plaintext.

30
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:26,247
Now it registers the analysis task on-chain.

31
00:01:26,247 --> 00:01:29,372
The encrypted payload goes to the TEE node,

32
00:01:29,372 --> 00:01:32,782
which performs the analysis inside the enclave.

33
00:01:32,782 --> 00:01:34,222
And here is the result.

34
00:01:34,222 --> 00:01:37,907
Risk score, per-asset rebalancing advice, and a

35
00:01:37,907 --> 00:01:41,899
summary, decrypted locally, and only visible to me.

36
00:01:42,450 --> 00:01:46,041
At the bottom, the app proves end-to-end integrity.

37
00:01:46,041 --> 00:01:49,494
The attestation's result hash matches the decrypted

38
00:01:49,494 --> 00:01:52,616
payload, signed by the registered TEE key, and

39
00:01:52,616 --> 00:01:55,538
anchored by the registry contract on Flare.

40
00:01:55,538 --> 00:01:58,500
Everything you see was built during this hackathon.

41
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:02,173
The TEE engine, the Coston2 contracts, and this

42
00:02:02,173 --> 00:02:03,704
encrypted frontend.

43
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:07,074
Next, we plan to pull FTSO price feeds

44
00:02:07,074 --> 00:02:10,427
directly inside the enclave, add zero-knowledge

45
00:02:10,427 --> 00:02:13,850
risk proofs for lending protocols, and launch on

46
00:02:13,850 --> 00:02:14,897
Flare mainnet.

47
00:02:14,897 --> 00:02:16,297
Try the live demo.

48
00:02:16,297 --> 00:02:17,492
Links are below.

49
00:02:17,492 --> 00:02:18,308
Thank you!

